摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"ClawTouch MCP server — exposes a real USB-HID keyboard/mouse (Raspberry Pi Pico 2) as Model Context Protocol tools for any LLM agent. MIT.","id":"gh:1256365926","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"clawtouch-mcp","slug":"tinqiao-oss/clawtouch-mcp","topics":["ai-agent","anthropic","automation","claude","computer-use","dsh","dsh-plugin","hid","llm","mcp","model-context-protocol","rp2350","usb-hid"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"ClawTouch MCP server — exposes a real USB-HID keyboard/mouse (Raspberry Pi Pico 2) as Model Context "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"Protocol tools for any LLM agent. MIT."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"# clawtouch-mcp"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"> **Give your AI agent real hands.**\n> An MCP server that turns any MCP-compatible client — Claude D"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"esktop,\n> Cline, Continue,\n> Cursor, OpenClaw,\n> Hermes Agent and any other —\n> into something that "},{"id":"p4s3","text":"can move a real mouse and press real keys through a USB HID device."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## What is this?"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"A standalone Python process that speaks **Model Context Protocol** (MCP) over\nstdio and exposes mous"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"e / keyboard primitives — `hid.click`, `hid.type`,\n`hid.scroll`, key combos, `hid.screenshot` — to w"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"hatever AI agent you already\nuse. Under the hood it talks over USB serial to a **ClawTouch HID devic"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"e** (a\nRaspberry Pi Pico 2 running the open ClawTouch HID firmware, or any\nturnkey ClawTouch box) an"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"d translates each tool call into a real USB HID report.\nThe target OS sees a **genuine physical keyb"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"oard and mouse** — input arrives on\nthe same driver path as any plugged-in peripheral, not as a soft"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"ware-injected\nsynthetic event."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"> 📦 MIT-licensed. No ClawTouch backend, no LLM, no agent loop on top —\n> just the raw HID plumbing s"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"o other agent stacks can talk to real hardware."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> ⚠️ This gives an agent **real keyboard / mouse reach** over a machine —\n> the same reach as a pers"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"on at the keyboard. Read Safety first."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Why hardware HID?"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Software automation (PyAutoGUI, OS-level input APIs, multimodal click-the-screen\nmodels) injects **s"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"ynthetic** input events into a session — which requires an\nagent process running on the target machi"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"ne, in that user session, with focus.\nA USB HID peripheral works the other way around: it emits **re"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"al** HID reports\nthat travel the standard OS HID driver stack, exactly like a plugged-in keyboard\nor"},{"id":"p10s5","text":" mouse. The OS recognizes the Pico natively as a standard USB HID class device\nand needs **no mouse "},{"id":"p10s6","text":"/ keyboard driver and no HID agent process** on the input\nside of the target. That difference is the"},{"id":"p10s7","text":" whole point of this project — every\nother section below just builds on it."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**The board acts on the machine it is plugged into.** It takes its commands\nover the same USB cable "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"it types through, so `clawtouch-mcp` runs on that\nmachine too — the input side still needs no driver"},{"id":"p11s3","text":". The agent itself can run\nelsewhere; see Deployment modes."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**Good for:**"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- **Kiosks / locked-down machines** — no input driver or input agent to\ninstall or keep running: the"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" board is a standard USB keyboard and mouse\n(`clawtouch-mcp` itself runs on the machine).\n- **Access"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"ibility** — let a user drive their own computer via an agent issuing\nHID commands, without fighting "},{"id":"p13s4","text":"per-app synthetic-input compatibility.\n- **Compatibility testing** — verify your software handles *e"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"xternal* HID input\ncorrectly, which can differ from injected synthetic events.\n- **Test rigs** — an "},{"id":"p13s6","text":"agent on your dev laptop drives a test machine that runs\n`clawtouch-mcp` (started over SSH, for exam"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"ple — see Deployment modes)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**Not for:**"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"- **Mass account creation / multi-account operations** — a single-host tethered\nperipheral is struct"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"urally a poor fit; one device drives exactly one target,\nand to drive ten machines you buy ten devic"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"es.\n- **Application-specific scripted shortcuts** (selectors, fixed-flow scripts for\na particular si"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"te or app). Those belong in agent / RPA frameworks built on top\nof this primitive layer, not in this"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"ose belong in agent / RPA frameworks built on top\nof this primitive layer, not in this layer itself."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"For standard desktop apps (browser, IDE, office suites) the software-only path\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Quickstart"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> ⚠️ Before you start: read Safety — a connected agent can operate this machine like a person at the"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"e you start: read Safety — a connected agent can operate this machine like a person at the keyboard."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### What an agent connected to this can do"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"`clawtouch-mcp` turns your agent's tool calls into **real USB HID input** — the\nsame property that m"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"akes the legitimate use cases work (kiosks, accessibility,\ncompatibility testing, test rigs) carries"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"e use cases work (kiosks, accessibility,\ncompatibility testing, test rigs) carries a symmetric risk:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"**An autonomous agent connected here has, in practice, the same reach over the\nhost as a person sitt"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"ing at the keyboard.** It can open any application, run\ncommands in a terminal, install or remove so"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"ftware, and read, move, or delete\nfiles. Because the input arrives as ordinary HID, a confirmation p"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"rompt is not\nby itself a reliable barrier — treat any consent dialog as something the agent\nmay act "},{"id":"p21s5","text":"on. `clawtouch-mcp` does **not** inspect intent or content; it\nfaithfully forwards each call to the "},{"id":"p21s6","text":"touch-mcp` does **not** inspect intent or content; it\nfaithfully forwards each call to the hardware."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"This can happen **without you intending it**, because the *agent* decides what\nto do. The usual trig"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"can happen **without you intending it**, because the *agent* decides what\nto do. The usual triggers:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"- **Prompt injection.** Untrusted text the agent reads off the screen, a web\npage, or an image can c"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"arry instructions that override yours.\n- **Model error.** The model misunderstands the task and acts"},{"id":"p23s3","text":" on the wrong\nwindow, file, or button.\n- **Over-broad autonomy.** The more open-ended the task and t"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"he fewer the\ncheckpoints, the larger the blast radius."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"This is an **unintended failure mode**, not a supported use — deliberately\nusing HID input to defeat"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" a system's security controls is out of scope under\n**Acceptable use** below. It is also distinct fr"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"om software bugs in\n`SECURITY.md`: none of those cover an agent acting against your\nown intent. The "},{"id":"p24s4","text":"MIT \"AS IS / no warranty\" clause is a liability disclaimer, not\nan informed-risk notice; responsibil"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"ity for running an autonomous agent safely\nsits with you as the deployer. This notice is provided fo"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"r information only —\nit does not modify, narrow, or expand the MIT License, create any warranty or\nd"},{"id":"p24s7","text":"uty of care, or shift liability to Tinqiao; the MIT no-warranty / no-liability\nterms continue to gov"},{"id":"p24s8","text":" or shift liability to Tinqiao; the MIT no-warranty / no-liability\nterms continue to govern in full."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Architecture overview"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"This repo is the MCP-server hop: it translates MCP tool calls into framed bytes over USB-CDC; the fi"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"rmware turns them into standard USB HID reports."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
